## read.tucson() is built on data.table.  These imports are not merely a
## convenience: data.table's cedta() check decides whether `[.data.table`
## dispatches to the data.table method or falls back to `[.data.frame`, and it
## answers TRUE for a package only if that package imports data.table in its
## NAMESPACE.  Without this block the `:=` calls inside read.tucson() would
## silently do the wrong thing.  See
## vignette("datatable-importing", package = "data.table").
importFrom(data.table, data.table, as.data.table, fread, melt, dcast,
           rbindlist, setorder, setcolorder, uniqueN, fifelse, copy,
           ":=", ".SD", ".N", ".I")


